WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:05.420
It's been quite the journey, but WandaVision
has reached its final episode.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:10.900
What began as a love letter to classic TV
slowly transformed into a tale of confusion,

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.950
betrayal, grief and more.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:17.490
Here's how WandaVision wrapped up its small-screen
tenure, and what the finale means for the

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:18.490
MCU's future.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:24.221
After holding Wanda's twin sons hostage and
forcing her to relive her past trauma, Agatha

00:00:24.221 --> 00:00:26.859
continues her pursuit of Wanda's power.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:31.919
As noted in last week’s episode, Wanda is
apparently the legendary Scarlet Witch -- a

00:00:31.919 --> 00:00:37.840
being capable of unmatched creation and destruction
-- so naturally, Agatha is prepared to go

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.769
to great lengths to take Wanda's Chaos Magic
for herself.

00:00:41.769 --> 00:00:46.289
The two battle in the series finale, using
their abilities against one another, but Wanda

00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:47.770
is effectively powerless.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:52.149
Every time she tries to fight back against
Agatha, the ancient witch absorbs the energy

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:53.309
for herself.

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:58.179
This leads Wanda to get crafty -- witchcrafty,
if you will -- sneaking up from behind and

00:00:58.179 --> 00:01:03.550
using the mind-control trick she used back
in her first appearance in 2015's Avengers:

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:04.550
Age of Ultron.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:09.670
Her illusion sends Agatha back to the day
she killed off her witch coven, though the

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:13.250
seasoned magic-user quickly turns the spell
around on her.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:18.170
In response, Wanda breaks it and takes the
fight to Agatha directly, before seemingly

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:20.950
giving up and handing over her Chaos Magic
willingly.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:26.341
Her body turns dark and withered and Agatha
gains the strength she desires, but Wanda

00:01:26.341 --> 00:01:28.320
has one more trick up her sleeve.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.920
Wanda reveals that she placed runes on the
interior walls of the Hex, and regains the

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.280
lifeforce it seemed Agatha had drained from
her.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.210
Just as Agatha taught her, only the witch
who cast them can use their magic in a confined

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.210
space.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:47.700
This gives her the chance to reabsorb her
power and take the form of the Scarlet Witch,

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.490
overpowering her enemy.

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:53.619
Defeated and desperate, Agatha pleads with
Wanda to no avail, forced to live out her

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:57.060
days in her chatty alter-ego, Agnes.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.179
It's rare for villains to outlive their introduction
in the MCU, so it's pretty much a given that

00:02:02.179 --> 00:02:04.600
Agatha will return somewhere down the line.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.920
In fact, it seems almost like a guarantee.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:07.920
"You're gonna need me."

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.340
"If I do, I know where to find you."

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.790
The only question left now is just how soon
we'll see her again -- in Doctor Strange in

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:17.910
the Multiverse of Madness?

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.350
Or somewhere further down the line?

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:26.100
A major surprise came at the tail end of WandaVision's
eighth episode, unveiling S.W.O.R.D.'s "White

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.590
Vision" for the first time.

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:32.070
The synthezoid specter got the chance to show
off what he can do this week, nearly crushing

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:36.420
Wanda's skull and going head-to-head with
the Hex-bound Vision of her creation.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.080
The majority of the two Visions' confrontation
gives longtime Marvel fans the kind of laser

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:45.940
beam-shooting, hand-to-hand action they've
been waiting for, but not for long.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:50.400
After clashing for a short while, the Visions
share an intellectual debate concerning the

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.260
nature of their existence.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:57.980
Levitating inside Westview's library, Vision
presents White Vision with the Ship of Theseus

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:59.150
thought experiment.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:03.800
The theory asks that if the ship's rotting
pieces are continually replaced over time,

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:08.240
does the ship eventually cease to exist, since
its original form will eventually be depleted?

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.370
“I request elaboration.”

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:15.720
They apply that question to themselves, noting
that Westview's Vision lacks a physical form

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.310
but contains the Vision's soul, and White
Vision retains the original's synthetic body

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:24.370
and memories, filed away as "data" in his
"memory storage,” but doesn't have the Vision's

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.370
personality.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.470
Therefore, are either of them truly Vision?

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:30.170
“Neither is the true ship.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:34.120
Both are the true ship.”

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:39.060
To put this debate to bed, the Wanda-created
Vision unlocks his double's memories, who

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:43.270
has realized that the knowledge of his true
self was being suppressed by Hayward, in order

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:46.340
to make him "a weapon to be more easily controlled."

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:51.050
With his data restored, the White Vision leaves
Westview and disappears for the rest of the

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:52.050
series finale.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:55.790
But it's safe to assume that he'll make his
return in a future MCU project.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:04:00.160
When -- and whether or not he'll attempt to
reconnect with Wanda -- are questions only

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:01.380
time can answer.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:08.250
In the midst of their magic-slinging confrontation,
Agatha begins to play some serious mind games

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.500
with Wanda.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:14.450
This includes her awakening a handful of Westview's
residents, leading them to surround Wanda

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:15.630
and beg for mercy.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:20.560
They say they share in her pain and either
want to be freed or die because the suffering

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.750
that comes with living under her trance is
unbearable.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:28.889
This causes Wanda to panic, so she opens the
Hex and allows the people to escape her clutches

00:04:28.889 --> 00:04:34.870
-- that is, until she notices Vision, Billy,
and Tommy disintegrating, as their existences

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:36.699
are tied to the Hex.

00:04:36.699 --> 00:04:41.630
Later on, with Agatha defeated and the Hex
completely wiped from Westview, the townspeople

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:46.430
still seem to hold plenty of ill-will toward
Wanda, shooting her the stink-eye on her way

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.770
out of the community.

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:53.219
Thankfully, Jimmy Woo and an FBI task force
show up to help the now-freed residents, but

00:04:53.219 --> 00:04:56.520
that doesn't absolve Wanda of her wrongdoings.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.819
She held an entire town against their will
and unwittingly caused them real harm for

00:05:00.819 --> 00:05:02.400
quite a long time.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.620
That's something that doesn't go away in the
blink of an eye, and Wanda's guilt will likely

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:11.509
last just as long as the psychological damage
she caused for every one of them.

00:05:11.509 --> 00:05:16.130
Chances seem good that we'll be hearing about
Westview again in a future MCU project soon

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:22.240
-- just as the consequences of the battles
in Sokovia and Lagos reverberated after Avengers:

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:25.689
Age of Ultron and Captain America: Civil War.

00:05:25.689 --> 00:05:29.810
After it briefly appeared in WandaVision's
seventh installment, "Breaking the Fourth

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:33.482
Wall," viewers finally got a good look at
Agatha's magical book, the Darkhold.

00:05:33.482 --> 00:05:37.560
"That's the book of the damned."

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:42.250
The longtime witch first mentions it by name
in the series finale, telling Wanda that the

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:47.370
Darkhold contains an entire chapter devoted
solely to the Scarlet Witch -- a powerful

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:51.000
sorceress who defies the usual rules of witchcraft.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.129
Agatha notes that it's Wanda's destiny to
destroy the world.

00:05:54.129 --> 00:05:58.669
This moment must've piqued Wanda's interest,
as she's shown reading the so-called "Book

00:05:58.669 --> 00:06:02.099
of the Damned" in the show's final post-credits
scene.

00:06:02.099 --> 00:06:07.090
Unsurprisingly, the Darkhold is a storied
artifact from the pages of Marvel Comics,

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:12.460
dating back to 1972's Marvel Spotlight #4,
where it's described as a collection of spells

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:14.689
and techniques of dark magic.

00:06:14.689 --> 00:06:19.470
Over the years, the Darkhold has had many
owners -- including the sorceress Morgan Le

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:24.300
Fay, who bound it from a collection of parchments
into the unholy book it would become, and

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.180
even the Sorcerer Supreme, Doctor Strange.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:31.620
Considering both Wanda's devotion to understanding
the Darkhold's knowledge and Doctor Strange's

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:36.310
comic history as one of its previous owners,
it's a safe bet that the Darkhold is coming

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:40.389
with her when she shows up in Doctor Strange
in the Multiverse of Madness.

00:06:40.389 --> 00:06:44.749
And given the fact that she hears her kids
crying for help as she reads through the book

00:06:44.749 --> 00:06:48.550
in the scene's final moments, there's a pretty
good chance she'll seek out the good doctor's

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:53.069
help so she can rescue them from whatever
dimension they may now be trapped within.

00:06:53.069 --> 00:06:58.349
As Marvel Comics fans may recall, Billy and
Tommy are revealed to be shards of a demon's

00:06:58.349 --> 00:07:01.379
soul in 1989's ﻿Avengers West Coast﻿ #52.

00:07:01.379 --> 00:07:06.849
Could the MCU's take on Wanda's powerful progeny
be trapped in Hell itself?

00:07:06.849 --> 00:07:11.620
Of course, devoted fans know that this isn't
the first time we've seen the Darkhold in

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:12.620
the MCU.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.840
Its first screen appearance was actually in
season four of Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:22.279
There, it was established that the shape-changing
book has long been a powerful artifact in

00:07:22.279 --> 00:07:27.099
the MCU, and it wound up playing a large role
in the Phil Coulson-led team's dealings with

00:07:27.099 --> 00:07:30.419
the newest version of Ghost Rider, among other
shenanigans.

00:07:30.419 --> 00:07:35.419
It next appeared in the late, lamented hulu
original Runaways, and was wielded by the

00:07:35.419 --> 00:07:38.070
evil sorceress Morgan le Fay.

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:42.749
Just how the book ended up in Agatha's possession
-- or even if Marvel Studios will recognize

00:07:42.749 --> 00:07:47.190
its previous appearances in the now-defunct
Marvel Television productions -- remains to

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.190
be revealed.﻿﻿

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:53.800
After a week away from the WandaVision spotlight,
Monica Rambeau had a bit more to do in "The

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:54.889
Series Finale."

00:07:54.889 --> 00:07:59.560
Not only did Monica take down Agatha's fake
take on Quicksilver, who's neither a recast

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:04.589
version of the MCU Pietro, nor the X-Men version
from a different universe -- Instead, he's

00:08:04.589 --> 00:08:08.319
actually just some guy named Ralph Bohner.

00:08:08.319 --> 00:08:09.930
"Bohner."

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:13.469
But Monica also got to test out her burgeoning
powers.

00:08:13.469 --> 00:08:16.159
With the Hex down, Director Hayward and his
S.W.O.R.D.

00:08:16.159 --> 00:08:18.100
cronies burst on the scene.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:22.379
When Hayward fires his gun at Wanda's kids
Billy and Tommy, Monica steps in.

00:08:22.379 --> 00:08:27.490
She uses her phasing abilities to alter her
physiology, thus stopping the bullets from

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:28.610
hitting the twins.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:34.380
With the help of Darcy Lewis, Hayward is apprehended
and his plan is foiled, leaving Jimmy Woo

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.600
and Monica Rambeau to clean up Westview.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:41.890
In the first of the WandaVision finale's two
post-credits scenes, a S.W.O.R.D.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:45.760
agent ushers Monica into the local movie theater
to speak with her.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:50.560
Revealing herself to be a Skrull, the agent
mentions that an old friend of Monica's mother,

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:54.390
Maria Rambeau, sent her and wants to arrange
a meeting.

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:59.520
When asked where, the Skrull then points upward,
indicating that their conversation will take

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:01.120
place in space.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:05.340
Could this be a follow-up to the end-credits
scene from Spider-Man: Far From Home, where

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:09.400
Nick Fury is shown sitting comfortably aboard
a massive, Skrull-filled spacecraft?

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:13.960
Or is the Skrull referring to the return of
Talos?

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:18.630
Alternatively, is this a setup for Monica's
inclusion in Captain Marvel 2 via a reunion

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:19.860
with Carol Danvers?

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:23.210
Time will tell, but it's clear that Monica's
story is far from over.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:29.710
In keeping with the series of unending tragedies
that is Wanda Maximoff's life, her perfect

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:35.080
fictional world finally comes crashing down
at the end of the WandaVision series finale.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:40.300
With Agatha defeated, the people of Westview
freed, and S.W.O.R.D. as well as the FBI on

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:44.700
her case, Wanda is left no other choice but
to take down the Hex.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:49.410
Streets and shops begin returning to their
natural state, and the time of day once again

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:51.270
matches the outside world.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:56.710
The disintegrating Hex closes in on the family,
and Wanda knows it's inevitable that Billy,

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:59.590
Tommy, and Vision will disappear from existence.

00:09:59.590 --> 00:10:04.520
Before that happens, the family returns home
after a long day of battle, begrudgingly prepared

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.590
to bid one another farewell.

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:11.450
First, Wanda and Vision tuck their twins into
bed, and she thanks them for choosing her

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:15.150
as their mother as the Hex's borders draw
nearer.

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:19.560
Wanda and Vision then enter the living room
to say their final goodbyes to each other.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:24.610
Wanda reveals this Vision exists thanks to
the elements of the Mind Stone that live inside

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:25.610
of Wanda.

00:10:25.610 --> 00:10:29.840
They embrace, with the synthezoid predicting
that, much like before, they'll meet again

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:31.570
someday in some form.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:36.650
He then disappears, leaving Wanda alone once
again on the plot of land where they once

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:38.100
planned to build their home.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:44.020
On paper, WandaVision is a tough sell: It's
about a powerful witch who crafts a fake reality

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:48.750
to avoid properly grieving the loss of her
true love, who was previously killed -- twice

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.590
-- several movies ago.

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:55.800
Couple that with Wanda and Vision's super-powered
children, the recast Pietro Maximoff, the

00:10:55.800 --> 00:11:00.560
people Wanda took hostage, Agatha's whole
deal in general, S.W.O.R.D.'s status as mostly

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:05.820
good guys but also partially bad guys, and
the weird-factor only increases.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:10.220
Even still, the cast and crew involved managed
to turn this risky premise into something

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:12.370
truly special.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:16.880
WandaVision made fans laugh, cry, and everything
in between, and is sure to spark conversation

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:19.390
and debate for a good long time to come.

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:24.250
If this is the level of quality viewers can
expect from Marvel Studios' Disney+ offerings,

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:27.580
then the MCU's future is very bright, indeed.

